@startuml A2_2_intercore_contracts
title Figma Sketch · A2.2 · Межъядерные контракты
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
package "C1 · Editor" as C1 {
 interface "DocumentPort\nload / apply / revision" as DocPort
 interface "SyncPort\nsubmit / receive / ack / catch-up" as SyncPort
 interface "LockPort\nacquire / renew / release / validate" as LockPort
 interface "AssetPort\nupload / download / checksum" as AssetPort
 interface "CommentAnchorPort\ncreate / update / resolve anchor" as AnchorPort
}
package "C2 · Sync" as C2 {
 component "Operation Service" as OpSvc
 component "Lock Service" as LockSvc
 component "Presence / Signaling" as Presence
}
package "C3 · Storage" as C3 {
 component "Document / Version Store" as DocStore
 component "Asset Store" as AssetStore
 component "Backup / Restore" as Backup
}
package "C4 · Communication" as C4 {
 component "Comment Threads / Chat" as Threads
 component "Call Service" as Calls
 component "Recording / Summary Jobs" as Jobs
}
DocPort --> C1
SyncPort --> OpSvc
LockPort --> LockSvc
AssetPort --> AssetStore
AnchorPort --> Threads
OpSvc <--> DocStore : durable operation log / snapshot metadata
OpSvc <--> LockSvc : lock validation context
Presence <--> Calls : presence / signaling
Threads --> DocStore : comment anchor references
Calls --> Jobs : recording / transcript / summary jobs
Jobs --> C3 : persist recordings, transcripts, summaries
note bottom of SyncPort
 Contract requires unique operationId, idempotency,
 base revision, ordering metadata, acknowledgements,
 reconnect cursor and remote operation delivery.
end note
note bottom of LockPort
 Lease has owner, token, expiry and renewal.
 Expired/disconnected client loses edit authority.
end note
note bottom of C3
 Contract requires versioned documents/assets,
 checksums, backup and point-in-time restore.
 Exact RPO/RTO and retention are configuration decisions.
end note
note bottom of C4
 Calls must not block editor availability.
 Recording uploads are chunked/resumable;
 AI summaries are retryable durable jobs.
 Comment thread text/replies live in C4;
 C1 owns anchor coordinates/references.
end note
note right of Calls
 TURN/STUN and real-time media transport
 are connectivity infrastructure, not durable storage.
end note
@enduml
